        "id": "org:the-anchor",
        "type": "Organisation",
        "name": "The Anchor",
        "aliases": [
          "The Anchor Pub",
          "The Anchor Stanwell Moor"
        ],
        "description": "Independent British village pub and restaurant located on Horton Road, Stanwell Moor, Surrey. It is the closest traditional pub to Heathrow Airport (about seven minutes from Terminal 5, about 11 minutes from Terminals 2 & 3, and about 12 minutes from Terminal 4 — all times traffic dependent)【819931593353551†L64-L83】. The pub offers free on‑site parking for around 20 cars【819931593353551†L64-L73】, sits outside London’s ULEZ zone【819931593353551†L64-L73】 and features a plane‑spotting beer garden directly under the Heathrow flight path【882664815234677†L50-L113】. The Anchor markets itself as an inclusive community hub that welcomes families, women, dog owners, local residents and travellers alike and regularly hosts quiz nights, cash bingo, drag cabaret and other events.",
